    "not_introduced_by": "f1fc4d42eb60bddd59ae18e2a2797e55e1c80c7c",
    "mechanism": "Unconditional unknown-length upload EOF wait precedes response headers; W7 consumers require a flushed prefix to release upload completion/failure, so the wait deadlocks and becomes a 502 or timeout."
  },
  "contracts": [
    "Known oversized uploads reject before forwarding with 413.",
    "Unknown oversized uploads detected before response headers retain 413, including an early empty 200 or bodyless 204.",
    "A nonempty response prefix can progress before request EOF; subsequent upload read or size-limit errors abort the downstream response with unexpected EOF.",
    "A completed streamed response owns cleanup of an unfinished upload.",
    "HTTP/1 keep-alive enables full duplex so net/http does not drain the request before flushing the response."
  ],
